    "finalText": "Done. The implementation is complete and verified:\n\n- **`app/`** — FastAPI app: `config.py` reads `DATABASE_URL` via pydantic-settings (no hard-coded credentials), `db.py`/`models.py` use SQLAlchemy with a `links` table (unique code, url, clicks, creation order via autoincrement id), `schemas.py` validates absolute http/https URLs with a host and 4–20 char `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` codes, `main.py` implements the endpoints with `{\"error\": ...}` handlers for 422/404/409 and an atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` increment for redirects.\n- **Alembic** migration `0001_create_links` applies on startup; **`start.sh`** (executable) runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves `uvicorn` on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground; **`requirements.txt`** pins the stack versions; **README** documents `sh start.sh`.\n\nVerified end-to-end: full HTTP suite passed twice (201/409/422/404/302 with exact Location, single click increments, list ordering, unique generated codes), restart persistence kept click counts, cold start migrated from an empty DB, test data wiped, and port 8000 is free for the grader."
